# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep host artefacts out of it.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that matters: it carries `better-sqlite3` compiled for
# whatever libc the workstation runs. Copied into an Alpine image it would either be
# overwritten by the install — wasting a few hundred megabytes of context on every
# build — or, worse, shadow it and fail at runtime with an error about a missing
# shared library.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

.git
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml
.idea
.vscode

# Runtime data: the SQLite file, transfers in flight, the gateway keypair.
var
packages/api/data
**/.env.local

docs
*.md
!README.md
